    {
      "text": "They tell us how many pieces of a whole we have, and how many pieces make up the whole thing."
    }
  ],
  "explore": {
    "scenario": "Imagine we are running a busy bakery right before a big festival! We've just baked a delicious, giant cake, but we need to share it fairly among all the customers who are waiting eagerly. How do we make sure everyone gets an equal share?",
    "points": [
      {
        "text": "Teacher draws a large circle on the blackboard, representing the whole cake.",
        "detail": "Emphasize that this is one whole, undivided cake."
      },
      {
        "text": "Ask students: 'If I want to share this cake with one friend, how many equal pieces do I need to cut it into?' (Solicit 'two'.)",
        "detail": "Guide them to understand the concept of dividing a whole into equal parts."
      },
      {
        "text": "Teacher then draws lines to divide the 'cake' into two, then four, then eight equal parts, asking how many pieces each time and writing the fraction for one piece (1/2, 1/4, 1/8) next to it.",
